From 94c84ff027c5720e68dfa503914cbc4851fb77e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qzshch <qzshch@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:17:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] feat(models): device placement transactions for sparse
 KV working sets

Add the storage-layer capability KVMem-style retrieval tiering builds on:

- KVExecutionTablePool::publish_holes writes kPagedKVPageHole for a logical
  page range whose device replicas are absent.
- LogicalKVPageStore::drop_device_replica_within_active drops an active
  sequence's device replica while keeping the page and its (current) Host
  replica; the caller guarantees the page is outside every in-flight unit's
  read/write set (notably not the growing tail).
- HostKVExtentStore::prepare gains pin_active_writers so an active sequence's
  committed pages can be flushed to Host at a GPU boundary.
- KVAddressSpaceStore::apply_device_placement atomically moves the device
  working set to a caller-chosen page set: outgoing pages are flushed to Host
  when stale and drop their replicas, incoming pages are restored from their
  current Host replicas (contiguous extent runs copy as one transfer), the
  execution row is republished with holes for non-selected pages, and the
  reservation is rebalanced to the working set plus growth. Defined
  out-of-class in host_kv_store.h to keep the store headers acyclic.

test_kv_placement covers demote/reselect/promote round-trips, block-table
hole publication, byte-exact Host-authority restore over corrupted device
pages, growth past the working set, and leak-free teardown.

